# The port: haxelib's client, as Haxe 4.3.7 ships it, compiled to C++ with Nekomata's
#  sources linked in, so that it runs library scripts in its own process. Writes
#  bin/haxelib, and bin/neko, the same executable standing in for neko.
#  tools/fetch.sh fetches haxelib/ and nekomata/ first
# haxelib reads its version from haxelib.json and .git in the folder it builds in, so
#  paths from here on are from haxelib/
--cwd haxelib
# haxelib's each.hxml, its client's class paths
each.hxml
-cp ../src
-cp ../nekomata/src
--main nekomata.haxelib.Main
--macro nekomata.haxelib.Patches.apply()
# What Nekomata's host.hxml builds its host with
-D scriptable
--dce no
# The runtime is only named by generated scripts, so nothing else pulls it in
--macro include("nekomata.rt")
-D HXCPP_CATCH_SEGV
-D HXCPP_STACK_TRACE
-D HXCPP_STACK_LINE
-D HAXE_OUTPUT_FILE=haxelib
# A scriptable build lists its classes in export_classes.info, by default in the folder
#  it builds in, which would leave haxelib/ changed and its version "dirty"
-D dll_export=../bin/cpp/export_classes.info
--cpp ../bin/cpp
--cmd haxe --cwd ../tools --run Install ../bin/cpp ../bin
